  universityChannels: 'Students holding Cambridge or Pearson Edexcel A-Levels, or an IB Diploma, access Italian universities through recognition rather than the Italian Maturita. CIMEA — Italy\'s ENIC-NARIC centre — issues a statement of comparability that universities use to assess the qualification, and has largely replaced the older Dichiarazione di Valore route issued by embassies, being both faster and fully digital. The IB Diploma is explicitly recognised as an equivalent foreign secondary qualification. One point worth planning for early: Italian universities expect 13 years of prior schooling, so a Cambridge A-Level route reaching Year 13 satisfies this cleanly, whereas a 12-year American high school diploma may require an additional year of study or a foundation year unless paired with sufficient AP results — this catches families out at application stage and is easier to plan around from Year 10. Non-EU applicants resident abroad also pre-enrol through the Universitaly portal. Restricted-access programmes (medicine, dentistry, architecture and others) require a national entrance examination regardless of qualification, and Italian-taught degrees require documented Italian proficiency, typically CILS B2, CELI 3, or PLIDA B2. Internationally, Cambridge A-Levels are accepted by universities in 160+ countries via UCAS (UK) or direct application. Smartious provides personalised university guidance across Italian (CIMEA and Universitaly), UK (UCAS), and US (Common Application) destinations.',
  cambridgeCardDescription: 'Smartious\'s primary offer for Italy families. Cambridge IGCSE (Years 10-11) and Cambridge A-Level (Years 12-13) delivered as live online classes on a CET/CEST-aligned schedule. Two things make this fit Italy specifically: the A-Level years fall after the Italian education obligation is discharged at 16, so they carry no annual esame di idoneita requirement, and A-Level reaching Year 13 satisfies the 13-year schooling expectation for Italian university entry.',
  britishCurriculumSuits: 'Italy families targeting the Cambridge IGCSE + A-Level pathway. Best fit for: (1) families who want the strongest position for Italian university entry via CIMEA, given the 13-year point, (2) families relocating from the UK maintaining British curriculum trajectory to UCAS, (3) families in regions where international provision is thin — Florence and rural Tuscany, Emilia-Romagna\'s Motor Valley towns, southern Italy, (4) rotational corporate, diplomatic, and military families needing curriculum portability.',
  britishCurriculumDelivery: 'Live online classes scheduled to land within the Italian school day given the 1-2 hour CET/CEST-EAT offset, small groups 4-6 students. Cambridge examinations at Cambridge-authorised international schools accepting external candidates, confirmed per session.',
  ibDiplomaSuits: 'Italy families targeting the IB Diploma\'s breadth — internationally mobile diplomatic, UN-agency, and military families, and families wanting a qualification CIMEA recognises directly for Italian university entry without the Maturita.',
  ibDiplomaDelivery: 'Live online IB DP classes across all six subject groups plus Theory of Knowledge and Extended Essay supervision.',
  americanCurriculumSuits: 'Italy families targeting US universities via Common Application — particularly the Naples military community and Florence\'s American academic community. Worth pairing with an early conversation about the 13-year point if Italian university entry is also a possibility.',
  americanCurriculumDelivery: 'American Curriculum with AP courses Grades 9-12, SAT/ACT preparation, Common App essay coaching.',
  founderBioCountrySpecific: 'Alfred Ouko founded Smartious in 2019 to make international qualifications (Cambridge, IB, American) accessible to families across emerging markets and international corporate rotational communities at online-delivery fees. Italy families join students in 22 other countries — from Milan\'s Brera to Nairobi\'s own Diamond Plaza HQ, Paris\'s Neuilly to Copenhagen\'s Nordhavn.',
  founderUniversitySpecialism: 'Alfred holds a BEd in Mathematics and Physics — Smartious\'s Cambridge A-Level and IB Diploma STEM subjects are led personally when needed, which suits Italy\'s engineering-heavy corporate communities in Turin and Emilia-Romagna. Head of Academics supervises curriculum delivery and university placement strategy per family, including the CIMEA pathway for Italian university destinations.',

  competitorsIntro: 'Italy has a real international school landscape concentrated heavily in Milan and Rome, thinning markedly across Florence, Turin, Bologna, and the south. Fees at established schools typically run EUR 11,000-22,000/year. The dedicated online home-education market serving Italy is notably underdeveloped at upper-secondary level: the most visible provider stops at age 15, with no Cambridge IGCSE, A-Level, or IB continuation — leaving families with older teenagers to choose between a fee-paying campus, relocation, or nothing.',
